# a channel carries exactly one payload type. the constructor used to read
# only the first type argument, so Channel[Int, String](1) — likely someone
# expecting a pair payload — silently built a Channel[Int], and the
# three-argument spelling dropped two. both now report the same arity error
# the annotation position always gave.

fn main():
    ch := Channel[Int, String](1)
    ch.send(1)
    ch3 := Channel[Int, String, Bool](4)
    ch3.send(2)
    print("{ch.len()} {ch3.len()}")
